  'test-provider-error-remedies.js', // an error must name the RIGHT vendor's remedy. Both llm.js transient messages interpolated the provider NAME correctly and then hardcoded GOOGLE's links and Google's free-tier figures, so a live OpenRouter 429 read "Rate limit hit on OpenRouter … consider upgrading at ai.google.dev/pricing". It read as fixed since v3.0.4, which made the name dynamic and left the rest — a message that is right in one clause and wrong in the next is far harder to spot than one wrong throughout. Same shape in ingest.js, where an empty .md was answered with "run ocrmypdf". §3 drives the REAL retry ladder through the production injection seams (a "retryDelay" hint makes it wait 1ms, so nothing about the classification is stubbed and no paid call is made); §4 proves all five message-substring classifiers across four files still fire, because "(HTTP 429)"/"(HTTP 503)"/"temporarily overloaded" are read as TEXT by the batch queue, sharedbrain's strike counter and the CI flake gate — rewording them breaks a recovery path with nothing else going red. NO rate-limit FIGURES are printed: v3.15.0's rule that an unverifiable number on an error screen is worse than none.
  'test-model-failure-ux.js',     // WHAT THE USER SEES WHEN A MODEL FAILS. Reported on a FREE OpenRouter model: wait, then a full-width wall of red. Five defects under it. (1) The shared 429 message told a chat user about "a bulk operation such as a large ingest" — the v3.0.7 class, missed on this path; a POSITIVE CONTROL proves the detector fires on the clause that actually shipped. (2) The 429 never said the ladder had already run, on the path that waits LONGEST. (3) The two messages counted one ladder differently (503 said "4 times" as a hand-typed literal; there are 4 ATTEMPTS and 3 RETRIES) — both now derive from MAX_RETRIES, and the number is pinned as a LITERAL so an expectation cannot be read from the same constant the code reads. (4) THE REAL BUG: openrouter-adapter sets err.retryAfterSeconds from the upstream Retry-After and parseRetryDelay read only Gemini's two MESSAGE forms, so every OpenRouter rate limit silently took the 60s default THREE TIMES — §4 rebuilds the old reader and MEASURES that the OpenRouter message matches neither form, so the finding is evidenced rather than recalled. Honouring a hint made an unbounded sleep reachable, so the SLEEP is clamped to the 60s the 503 arm already used while the REPORTED figure stays unclamped (clamping it would print a wait the provider never asked for). (5) Presentation: the failure now renders recessed, width-capped and NOT in danger-red, with v3.18.0's "ask again with another model" reused at the point of failure. §7-§9 EXECUTE the shipped renderThreadOnly against a fake document — a guard driving failedModelNoteHtml alone would stay green if the error branch never called it, which is exactly how the re-ask control came to be absent. NO rate-limit figure is ever printed (v3.15.0's rule); the free-model sentence has ONE owner, proven by byte-equality between the waiting surface and the failure surface.
