  'test-next-settings-default-section.js', // Settings opened on "Providers & keys" instead of General, the FIRST sidebar entry — reported by the maintainer from the macOS menubar widget and reproduced equally from the in-app rail button, because both resolve to the same navigate('settings') -> onEnter -> freshState(). ONE cause, not two: freshState hardcoded `section: 'providers'` and justified it in a comment as matching a design prototype, a value nobody updated when the sidebar order was finalised with General first. It was never a persisted last-section feature — the section is deliberately in-memory only, so there was no user intent to honour. The default is now DERIVED from SETTINGS_SECTIONS[0][0] at BOTH the default and the mount-time prefetch, so the sidebar's order and the landing section cannot drift apart again by editing one of them. The suite EXECUTES freshState and evaluates onEnter's own prefetch argument rather than grepping for the literal 'general' — a test that pins the literal twice would pass against two sites that agree with each other and disagree with the sidebar — and it carries a control proving the comparator can report a MISMATCH, not merely a match.
