  'test-openrouter-model-layer.js', // v3.15.0 OpenRouter: the model layer's load-bearing guards, each mutation-proven RED for a BEHAVIOURAL reason. callProvider TOTALITY (the pre-v3.15.0 fall-through sent an unknown provider into the Anthropic client on the user's Anthropic key — the mutation constructs 17 mis-billed clients); free-model price POSTURE (a free model must stay unpriced, never {input:0,output:0}, which is truthy and makes createJob's budget cap inert — v3.3.0's bug re-armed); EXACT price conversion (naive parseFloat(s)*1e6 yields 0.09999999999999999 for a $0.10/Mtok model, and the composer pins the money formula to exact-dollar equality over 126 cases); build-lane enforcement at BOTH layers separately (a chat-only model measured emitting unrepairable JSON in 2 of 9 real ingest runs could be pinned as the BUILD model until this release); usage normalisation SUBTRACTING cached tokens (OpenRouter follows the Gemini convention, not Anthropic's — the mutation overstates input by 20.9x); adapter key redaction across every error branch with a canary carrying NO sk-or- prefix; and the HTTP-200 in-band finish_reason:'error' case, which a status-only classifier reads as success.
  'test-api-keys-contract.js',       // v3.45.0: the SEAM between GET /api/config/api-keys and the Providers & keys page, which is where this release's own defect lived. The route emitted `build.facts.measured` as a BOOLEAN and the view read `'curator'|'user'|null`; BOTH SUITES WERE GREEN — the route's asserted `=== true`, the view's fed fixtures written to the three-valued shape — and nothing drove the join. Same shape as v3.34.0's dropped warning and v3.36.0's two update paths. This suite boots the REAL router on an ephemeral loopback port, saves a synthetic key over the REAL POST route so a REAL build model resolves, and feeds the ACTUAL serialised JSON into the REAL view functions brace-matched out of settings.js — never a fixture on either side. Pins three fact-versus-absence splits that a client cannot recover once collapsed: `measured` names WHO (a boolean is renderable as only one of the two badges, so a model the USER qualified would have been badged as one The Curator measured); a FREE model's prices are null and carry a `free` flag beside them, so the page says the word rather than `$0.00` (a rate that does not exist — v3.3.1 shipped that figure) or a blank (indistinguishable from unpriced, asserted separately); and `catalogueCounts.batchHidden` is null when never synced, where a 0 would ASSERT none was found — false for 64 ids on the 2026-09-02 catalogue. Every needle is SCOPED to block 2's own chip markup, because the same words appear on the model list below and a bare phrase would be green whatever block 2 said. Mutation-proven both ways: reverting the route to a boolean reds 5, and making the view ignore `free` reds 1.
